# This file aims at containing list of robot files on which we want to perform a DRY RUN check
# In robot, DRY RUN is a mode where only basic checks on keywords existency are done
# but it is useful to detect interface breaks, typo errors in keywords, import missing,...
# And this is useful to launch a dry run when common parts of code are modified


# Syntax :
# This file is divided in section.
# Each section starts with a Feature line, then is followed by N lines of robot file
# Feature line has following syntax: FEATURE=<PathToFeatureDifFromTestSuite>
#   Example : FEATURE=RRM/ECE/UE_Call_Setup/5GC000636-D
# Then, lines after are only lines with name of robot file (inside the feature, so, without path)
#   Example : 5GC000636-D_ClassicalTestCases.robot

# Example for feature 1857 classical
# FEATURE=RRM/ECE/UE_Call_Setup/5GC001857-A
# 5GC001857-A_ClassicalTestCases_1_3_5.robot
# 5GC001857-A_ClassicalTestCases_30.robot
# 5GC001857-A_ClassicalTestCases_7_9_11.robot

# PUT HERE YOUR FEATURE WITH YOUR ROBOT FILES :
# =============================================

